**The error** (`logs/app.log:25107`):
```
ERROR [billing] invoice 88121 failed: TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'rate')
    at taxFor (src/tax.js:13:30)
    at invoiceTotal (src/invoice.js:9:15)
```

**Root cause:** The preceding line logs `country=at` (lowercase). `taxFor` did a raw `RATES[country]` lookup against uppercase keys (`AT`, `DE`, `FR`), so the lowercase code missed, returned `undefined`, and `.rate` threw. Every other invoice in the log passes an uppercase code, which is why this is the only failure.

**Fix** (`src/tax.js`): normalize the country code before lookup, and throw a descriptive error for genuinely unknown countries instead of a cryptic `TypeError`:
```js
export function taxFor(cents, country) {
  const entry = RATES[String(country).toUpperCase()];
  if (!entry) {
    throw new Error(`no VAT rate configured for country ${country}`);
  }
  return Math.round(cents * entry.rate);
}
```

I also added regression tests in `tests/tax.test.js` covering mixed-case codes and the unknown-country path. All 8 tests pass and `node scripts/build.mjs` reports `BUILD OK`. Changes are left uncommitted per rule 10.

